# CentrMark in prohelp

Sections may `content-ref` a `.cmk` body. Prohelp renders a terminal-oriented
plain-text subset: headings, lists, fenced code, `((` blockquotes), and
`::: directives`.

## Inline marks

Status: @badge[color="success"](Stable). Contact @mention[openshellorg] for
upstream CentrMark tooling.

::: tip [title="Authoring"]
Keep one CentrMark source and reference it from `help.sdl` with
`format "centrmark"` (or rely on the `.cmk` extension).
:::

- Prefer `.cmk` for OpenShell-authored help bodies
- Prefer Texinfo/man for GNU upstream docs
- Prefer AsciiDoc when the same file feeds Antora
